{"id": "EUVD-2026-86941", "enisaUuid": "bcd9a07f-05ce-3d53-bb82-c7e9d05ef29a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel: bound firmware ID by TLV length\n\nThe firmware ID is treated as a NUL-terminated string even though the\nTLV length is its only boundary. If the value does not contain a NUL\nterminator, snprintf() can read beyond the received response.\n\nLimit the conversion to the advertised TLV value length.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:35:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:14:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aef56a2bd5aa22808ce508605d7497d2b5e8eb5f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/058f56de5f48ba4b3be01526006ac83ce9e79f39", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a07b3024a927892dd46e7dfbed438e8834e24098", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac8aa9e0ec93a12a60230066f199f49c3b9aac3d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98110", "GHSA-7mj5-jcph-6x3p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "166a4aeb-1891-3ee7-a479-b079b3193b32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "164c62f958f8c7f0bde1e9a5a8677971c6f28205 <a07b3024a927892dd46e7dfbed438e8834e24098"}, {"id": "325ef686-058a-3333-8e85-e9588486c1ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "164c62f958f8c7f0bde1e9a5a8677971c6f28205 <aef56a2bd5aa22808ce508605d7497d2b5e8eb5f"}, {"id": "49b0e7fa-b536-3e01-a879-1d2160f7f90a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "7b7cc4db-743c-3835-b472-781d68835f7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "164c62f958f8c7f0bde1e9a5a8677971c6f28205 <058f56de5f48ba4b3be01526006ac83ce9e79f39"}, {"id": "7da0a32a-e77e-35ab-887d-4044d1ac1aab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "85206cb3-0293-3001-aed2-979984d36310", "product": {"name"